  "body": "Was stacked on #2843 (`issue/917-kernel-parity`). #2843 is merged as 7173bb44a, and the base of this PR is `main` now.\n\n## What changed\n\n- The app reads a STEP model through solidcore: `camcraft_geometry::step::parse` calls the kernel seam (`import_step_model`, then `machining_mesh` for each solid). `camcraft-app` gets no new edge to `camcraft-kernel`.\n- The truck mesh path of the app is removed: 11 `step_*` modules of `crates/app/src/geometry/import/` and the truck dependencies of `crates/app/Cargo.toml`.\n- A model over the facet budget is meshed again at a coarser chord. The kept chord goes to `coarse_mm` (#864).\n- Each closed solid lands as one facet range (`solids` in the project file, optional, no version step). The slicer and the winding check read the solids from the ranges.\n- The shared-edge rule (`shared_edge::solids_touch`) accepts an edge where two closed solids touch along a wall.\n- The 2D corner check reads a self-crossing leftover loop by the even-odd rule (`outer_fills`, bc5daa32d).\n- `pick/winding.rs` is split: the welder and the union-find move to `pick/winding/weld.rs` (no behaviour change).\n- The browser build refuses a STEP file by name.\n- Review fixes (head 853522f2e): the face winding check of the kernel reads at most 4 `ORIENTED_FACE` wrappers, its union-find has union by size and path compression, and it reads the cancel token of the import.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/917-solidcore-step.md`.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Fixture | Reading on this branch | Pinned by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `fig8.step` | 12590 facets (main 7974), deviation measured within the tolerance | `shoulder_adaptive.rs` (known-fail #2849), decision table \"#2844\" |\n| `fillet_corner.step` | 1866 facets; closed-form volume at the kernel; the bent-weight variant is refused at read (\"first #1289 at read: face #1228: weight: ... out of range\") | kernel `step_closed_form.rs`, app `import_step_closed_shell.rs` (3 tests) |\n| `bar_cross_holes.step` | reads through the kernel pcurves; the tilted cross hole is judged | kernel `step_closed_form.rs`, app `tilted_gouge.rs` |\n| `twisted_flank.step` | reads at 7999.857 mm3 (want 8000, tolerance 0.8 mm3), 5132 facets, full fidelity | kernel, geometry and app `step_twisted_flank` tests, app `import_step_twisted_flank.rs` |\n| `twisted_flank_off.step` | refused: \"#117 at read: pcurves failed on 1 of 3 faces; first: face #93: off the surface's range\" | the same three test files |\n\n## Changed, ignored and deleted pins\n\nThe decision file has the old reading, the new reading, the cause and the safety argument for each.\n\n- Changed: `import_step_closed_shell.rs`, `import_step_open_shell.rs` test 1, `import_step_guard.rs`, `import_step_guard_default_cap.rs`, `import_step_curve_guard.rs`, `import_step_corner_blend.rs`, `model_fidelity.rs`, `import_step_thread.rs`, `import_step_doubly_curved.rs`, kernel `machining_mesh_parity.rs`, `bore_facet_sagitta.rs`, `step_chord_units.rs`, ui `model_incomplete.rs`. See \"Changed pins\".\n- Restored on the final head (the old assert still holds): the excess floor of `model_fidelity.rs`; the face count and gap text of `import_step_guard_default_cap.rs`; the full \"used twice\" refusal of `import_step_guard.rs`.\n- Made hard on the final head: geometry `step_twisted_flank.rs` (no longer accepts Ok or Err); the bore 0.05 mm pins now assert the blocking warning (`gouge`, \"move N cuts past the finish surface\").\n- Deleted: the 100 `#[test]` of the removed truck modules. See \"Removed truck modules (100 `#[test]`)\". Four mesh laws with no pin on the new path are filed as #2903 (item 1, `Unmeasured::NoSurface`, is pinned now at the measure step).\n- Ignored with the known-fail marker:\n  - #2849: `lead_approach.rs` (2 tests), `shoulder_adaptive.rs` (1 test).\n  - #2844: `import_step_thread.rs` (1 test).\n  - #2845: `feature_edge_g1_join.rs` (1 test), `winding_align.rs` (1 test).\n- #2850 makes the same corner-check change. See \"#2850 and the corner check\" for the merge rule.\n\n## `#[test]` count\n\nAgainst `issue/917-kernel-parity`: 8660 -> 8587 (-73). The 100 tests of the removed truck modules go. 27 tests come in: `model_solid_ranges` 4, kernel `machining_mesh_open` 6, kernel lib `step_face_winding` 2, kernel `machining_mesh_bounds` 1, geometry `step_metre_unit` 1, `shared_edge` 3, `winding_align` 2, geometry `step_twisted_flank` 2, app `import_step_twisted_flank` 2, `bore_facet_sagitta` 1, `step_chord_units` 1, `lead_approach` 1, `unreached` 1. Ignored: 120 -> 125 (6 known-fail markers in, 1 heavy-lane ignore out with its module).\n\n## Gate\n\n- Batch gate on bc5daa32d: 951 steps, 0 failed, clippy clean.\n- Targeted runs on the final head 2ad350627 (debug, `-j 12`):\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-geometry --test step_twisted_flank`: 2 passed.\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test import_step_twisted_flank`: 2 passed.\n  - `--test bore_facet_sagitta`: 3 passed. `--test step_chord_units`: 4 passed.\n  - `--test winding_align`: 10 passed, 1 ignored (#2845). `--test import_step_outward`: 3 passed.\n  - `--test model_fidelity`: 9 passed. `--test import_step_guard`: 6 passed. `--test import_step_guard_default_cap`: 1 passed.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-geometry --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n- Review-fix runs on 853522f2e (debug, `-j 12`):\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-kernel --lib`: 8 passed (2 new: `a_hostile_edge_order_costs_linear_steps_and_keeps_each_parity`, `a_cancelled_winding_pass_stops_by_name`).\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-kernel --test machining_mesh_open`: 6 passed (2 new: `an_oriented_face_that_names_itself_returns_without_a_note`, `an_oriented_face_chain_past_the_limit_returns_without_a_note`).\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-kernel --test machining_mesh_bounds`: 5 passed (1 new: `a_face_with_no_surface_to_measure_is_refused_by_name`).\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-geometry --test step_metre_unit`: 1 passed.\n  - `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test model_fidelity`: 9 passed. `--test import_step_guard`: 6 passed. `--test import_step_curve_guard`: 3 passed.\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-kernel -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Follow-ups\n\n- #2909: a sheet gets no gap check, and an empty `left_out` gives a hole line with no face.\n- #2780 stays open: its speed item is held by #2844.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes (release, `--ignored`) were not run on this head.\n- The full batch gate was not run again after bc5daa32d. An independent gate-runner runs it.\n- No UI look changed, so no screenshots. The ui `model_incomplete` page test builds its open mesh in the test.\n\nChangelog: STEP models are now read by the solidcore kernel: each surface is meshed within a measured tolerance, faulty files are refused by name with the entity that fails, and touching solids import as separate bodies.\n\nRefs #917\nRefs #2780\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
